From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: msm8916-samsung-gt510: USB OTG with the MAX77849 boost

Let the USB controller switch roles, wired like the other Samsung MSM8916
boards with a MUIC (a2015, j5): the MAX77849 MUIC is the extcon for both
VBUS (EXTCON_USB) and ID (EXTCON_USB_HOST) of the controller and for the
VBUS of the HS PHY. The PMIC usbin extcon reported our own boost as VBUS
while in host mode.

5 V for the attached device comes from the charger boost, exposed by the
max77693 charger driver as an "otg-vbus" regulator that follows the
downstream Samsung sequence: CHG_CNFG_00 OTG|BOOST|DIS_MUIC_CTRL with
CHG+BUCK cleared, CHG_CNFG_11 VBYPSET 5 V, 1.2 A OTG current limit.
Flipping the MODE bits alone (0x5 <-> 0xa) left VBUS off.

While a USB host cable is attached the MUIC charger detection is turned
off; otherwise it detects the boosted VBUS as an SDP charger.

The MAX77849 reads STATUS1 bit 5 (ADCLow on MAX77693) as 1 both with ID
open and with ID grounded by an OTG cable, so the MUIC driver took a plain
OTG cable for an "AV cable with load" (audio path, EXTCON_USB): ignore
that bit on MAX77849.

The boost survives a reboot (the PMIC stays powered), and rebooting with
it on left the tablet dark with dead keys: switch it off at shutdown.
